  "customfield_10121": null,
  "customfield_10154": null,
  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I just started a 3.7.1 upgrade at Tufts as well.  While running the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "installer we ran into a different initial problem, and having resolved",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "that have caught up the problem reported here, so first off, thanks for",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "the info here in this thread.  The problem we initially hit is that in our",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "install we specify the low level storage option as legacy-fs, which upon",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "start up results in the following error:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "ERROR 13:46:21.014 (Server) Module",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.ILowlevelStorage) failed to initialize",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "org.fcrepo.server.errors.ModuleInitializationException: couldn't set up",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "path_algorithm for objectPaths  Class",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.defaultstore.Store can not access a",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "member of class org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.TimestampPathAlgorithm",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "with modifiers \"public\"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.DefaultLowlevelStorageModule.postInitMod",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "ule(DefaultLowlevelStorageModule.java:44) ~[fcrepo-server-3.7.1.jar:na]",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Looking at the fcrepo-server source it seemed to be related to this commit:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/commit/5ad360edf39bfeca57038974639b41073af1fd1b#diff-644ddc1704c65930c61becbd9826bee1"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/commit/5ad360edf39bfeca57038974639b41073af1fd1b#diff-644ddc1704c65930c61becbd9826bee1",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Where the Store class moved from being a support within",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "DefaultLowlevelStorage in the org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel package",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "to the org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.default package as a top level",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "class.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I confirmed that by making the TimestampPathAlgorithm class public this",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "issue goes away at startup since Store would then have access.  Not sure",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "if this is the correct fix or if Store should've stayed in the previous",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "package.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
